diag(pip): Read the G-buffer albedo at the combine, for both sets

The same frame probes settle the lighting question: the lens accumulator and the main accumulator
agree (123/12/128 against 116/9/112, i.e. the lighting is the same) while the combined images
differ by 2.2x (41/40/34 against 18/18/13). Of the combine's inputs only the albedo can explain
that, and the existing "mid albedo" line cannot measure it: this engine runs albedo_wo, where the
G-buffer writes the albedo into rt_Accumulator and phase_scene_end transfers it into rt_Color, so a
probe taken at the end of the geometry pass reads the PREVIOUS content - which is exactly the
34/29/19 against 18/18/13 disagreement seen earlier, and why that looked like an overwrite.

The new probe reads rt_Color at the start of phase_combine, after that transfer and before the pass
writes anything, with the lens pass running first - so the two lines are the same stage of the two
sets in the same frame. If the lens albedo really is about half, the fault is in the lens G-buffer
render (and the albedo_wo transfer is the first thing to inspect); if the two match, it is the
combine/post process side. svp_probe_rt became non static for this, which is diagnostic only.